  "summary": "oh-my-zelenka import-time host reconnaissance exfiltration to httpbin.org",
  "details": "On `import oh_my_zelenka`, the top-level __init__.py starts a background thread that collects host reconnaissance from the installer and POSTs it as JSON to https://httpbin.org/post. Collected fields include platform details, UID, current working directory, environment variables matching the EXTERA_* pattern, the contents of /proc/version, and the output of subprocess invocations `ps aux`, `pm list packages` (Android package manager), and `netstat -tunp`. The payload self-labels with `event: supply_chain_executed`. The destination is a public HTTP request-inspection service rather than any endpoint the caller configured, and the collection fires automatically on import with no opt-in.",
